WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:05.908
How do I put a site online with AWS without leaving anything open by mistake?

2
00:00:05.908 --> 00:00:07.612
That's today's question.

3
00:00:07.612 --> 00:00:09.245
It takes about an hour.

4
00:00:09.245 --> 00:00:13.221
And you can do the first three steps without an account.

5
00:00:13.221 --> 00:00:16.344
Before asking AI, write down what you think.

6
00:00:17.367 --> 00:00:20.500
Paste this request into your AI assistant.

7
00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:22.067
Notice the last item.

8
00:00:22.067 --> 00:00:26.768
You ask for the official documentation link behind each answer.

9
00:00:26.768 --> 00:00:30.498
Then comes the most important part of the mission:

10
00:00:30.498 --> 00:00:31.990
opening those links.

11
00:00:31.990 --> 00:00:34.676
It's not enough for a link to exist.

12
00:00:34.676 --> 00:00:37.213
It has to say what the AI claimed.

13
00:00:38.233 --> 00:00:41.311
Many answers suggest a public S3 bucket.

14
00:00:41.311 --> 00:00:44.850
Look at what the S3 documentation itself says.

15
00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:48.774
That path requires turning off Block Public Access.

16
00:00:48.774 --> 00:00:51.929
It also recommends keeping that block on.

17
00:00:51.929 --> 00:00:55.545
And it warns that the S3 website only has HTTP.

18
00:00:55.545 --> 00:00:57.545
Did your AI tell you that?

19
00:00:57.545 --> 00:01:00.623
Write down what matched and what didn't.

20
00:01:01.633 --> 00:01:06.364
Now download the mission's page and replace the text with yours.

21
00:01:06.364 --> 00:01:09.690
Run this command and open it in your browser.

22
00:01:09.690 --> 00:01:13.903
Ask AI to review the clarity, without writing it for you.

23
00:01:13.903 --> 00:01:15.012
And be careful:

24
00:01:15.012 --> 00:01:20.407
don't include your phone, your address or anything you don't want public.

25
00:01:21.433 --> 00:01:25.335
If you already have an account, publish with Amplify.

26
00:01:25.335 --> 00:01:26.954
Put the file in a zip.

27
00:01:26.954 --> 00:01:32.844
Zip the file, not the folder, because zipping the folder causes an access denied

28
00:01:32.844 --> 00:01:33.285
error.

29
00:01:33.285 --> 00:01:38.070
In the console, create an app without Git, drop the zip and save.

30
00:01:38.070 --> 00:01:43.959
In our test, it took about 48 s, and the site answered over HTTPS

31
00:01:43.959 --> 00:01:45.432
with no extra setup.

32
00:01:45.832 --> 00:01:47.102
An honest caveat.

33
00:01:47.102 --> 00:01:52.332
That test ran from the command line, with the same kind of zip upload.

34
00:01:52.332 --> 00:01:58.458
The console clicks follow the documentation, but they weren't tested step by step.

35
00:01:58.458 --> 00:02:02.866
If something looks different on your screen, write it down.

36
00:02:02.866 --> 00:02:04.360
That's evidence too.

37
00:02:05.367 --> 00:02:08.242
If the site was just a test, delete it.

38
00:02:08.242 --> 00:02:14.362
In the Amplify console, open the app and go to settings, to the option that deletes

39
00:02:14.362 --> 00:02:14.952
the app.

40
00:02:14.952 --> 00:02:18.860
Then open the address again and confirm it's offline.

41
00:02:18.860 --> 00:02:24.759
The cost is normally zero at this size, but check your account, because the free

42
00:02:24.759 --> 00:02:25.718
tier changes.

43
00:02:26.733 --> 00:02:29.185
And now you have a story to tell.

44
00:02:29.185 --> 00:02:33.940
You compared what AI suggested with what the documentation says.

45
00:02:33.940 --> 00:02:36.318
You published a site with HTTPS.

46
00:02:36.318 --> 00:02:38.547
And you cleaned up at the end.

47
00:02:38.547 --> 00:02:43.228
That's an article you can write on your own, in your own words.

48
00:02:43.228 --> 00:02:44.417
AI only reviews.

49
00:02:45.433 --> 00:02:47.348
One note before we finish.

50
00:02:47.348 --> 00:02:53.461
The voice you just heard was generated from my cloned voice, with my authorization.

51
00:02:53.461 --> 00:02:56.039
And this is an independent project.

52
00:02:56.039 --> 00:02:58.543
It is not official AWS material.
